import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About — Contractor License Lookup"
  description="Contractor License Lookup is an independent guide to checking contractor licenses with official state boards. How we research each state and how to reach us."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>About Contractor License Lookup</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      An independent, free guide to checking a contractor’s license with the official state board before you hire.
    </p>

    <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
    <p>
      Every state handles contractor licensing differently. Some license all contractors through one board, some split
      trades such as electrical and plumbing between several boards, and some leave general contractors to cities and
      counties. Finding the right official search takes time, and many sites that rank for it are out of date. We
      gather it in one place, state by state.
    </p>

    <h2>How we research each state</h2>
    <p>
      Every state guide is checked against the licensing board’s own website and published rules. Each page lists its
      sources and the date it was last checked. We add states only once they have been checked this way, and we
      re-check them as rules change.
    </p>

    <h2>We are not a government site</h2>
    <p>
      Contractor License Lookup is not affiliated with any state licensing board or government agency. License
      searches always happen on the official board’s website, which is the authoritative record.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Found something out of date, or want your state covered next? Email
      <a href="mailto:contact@contractorlicenselookup.org">contact@contractorlicenselookup.org</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
